WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.392
When a shopper narrows the catalog to more than one brand, the page should keep its usual title. Here the catalog opens filtered to both Daybird and Gravitator.

2
00:00:10.392 --> 00:00:19.568
With the products of both brands listed together, the header still reads Ready for a new adventure?, the usual title, rather than naming a single brand.

3
00:00:19.568 --> 00:00:27.827
Under it is the usual subtitle about starting the season, and there is no All brands link, because this is not a single brand's page.

4
00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:35.827
In the Brand filter, both Daybird and Gravitator are marked active, showing the two-brand selection behind this view.

5
00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:42.955
Shoppers comparing several brands see an honest, general title instead of a label that names only one of them.
